  "articleBody": "There's nothing more frustrating than an 'easy access' drawer that's anything but! If your drawers are sticking, not opening all the way, or just generally fighting you, it defeats the whole purpose. Often, the problem boils down to installation errors. Maybe the slide length was wrong, so the drawer can't fully extend, or perhaps the slides weren't placed perfectly parallel to each other. Even tiny things, like screws that aren't flush or wood shavings getting caught in the mechanism, can cause issues. The biggest giveaway that something's off is when the drawer binds or won't open smoothly, preventing you from getting to those items in the back. If you've tried troubleshooting and you're still struggling, it's probably time to call in someone with experience. Especially if your cabinet opening is tight or you need that perfect alignment for seamless operation, a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can get your drawers back to being truly easy access.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}